<article class="env-lemma" id="0F7U">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F7U">Lemma <span data-tag="0F7U">15.97.9</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring and let $f, g \in A$ be nonzerodivisors. Let $M^\bullet $ be a complex of $A$-modules such that $fg$ is a nonzerodivisor on all $M^ i$. Then $\eta _ f\eta _ gM^\bullet = \eta _{fg}M^\bullet $. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The statement means that in degree $i$ we obtain the same submodule of the localization $M^ i_{fg} = (M^ i_ g)_ f$. We omit the details. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
