<article class="env-lemma" id="0GSR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GSR">Lemma <span data-tag="0GSR">15.97.10</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring and let $f \in A$ be a nonzerodivisor. Let $A \to B$ be a flat ring map and let $g \in B$ the image of $f$. Let $M^\bullet $ be a complex of $f$-torsion free $A$-modules. Then $g$ is a nonzerodivisor, $M^\bullet \otimes _ A B$ is a complex of $g$-torsion free modules, and $\eta _ fM^\bullet \otimes _ A B = \eta _ g(M^\bullet \otimes _ A B)$. </p>
